{
  "name": "vector_light_shader_max_penumbra",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "\u00a727 phase 6 on a scene where BOTH halves are live. The open-door scene proves the level half but cannot test the shadow half at all: a sealed room with no interior obstruction gives the mask nothing to subtract, and its frame comes back byte-identical to vanilla \u2014 as it should. This is #151's room, which has two interior wall stubs casting real shadows plus a one-cell gap in the east wall, so the mask has darkness to carve while the shader sets the level. Four arms: vanilla, the mask alone, the mask plus the shipped flat beam, and phase 6. penumbra_area is pinned either side to prove the composition moves no geometry, and the question the numbers have to answer is whether the shader's additive pass refills the shadow the mask just cut \u2014 the flat beam gives back 0.35 L* of it, which is the bar phase 6 has to beat.",
